  "definition": "An ion thruster, in the narrow engineering sense used here, is a gridded electrostatic thruster. It creates a plasma inside a discharge chamber, extracts positive ions through closely spaced grids and accelerates them with a high electric potential. A neutraliser injects electrons into the exhaust so that the outgoing beam and spacecraft remain close to charge balance.[^1][^2]",
